# Release staging. release.sh writes the .s9pk, its SHA256SUMS and the detached
# signature here; the published record is the GitHub release, not the repo. Every
# sibling package ignores this. Without it a `git add -A` after a build sweeps the
# checksums in, which is how builds/3.3.1.24 through .34 came to be tracked.
builds/
